  BigFix Fixlet Export

  Title    : Upgrade Dell BIOS (Apr 2018, Intel Management Engine - Intel SA-00086) - Password Required
  ID       : 25505
  Author   : tdaker
  Domain   : BESC
  Imported : 2018-05-03T08:13:22
  Source   : bigfixm1_main @ BES-Root
-->
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>Upgrade Dell BIOS (Apr 2018, Intel Management Engine - Intel SA-00086) - Password Required</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<P>&nbsp;<LABEL for=secret><STRONG><FONT size=3>About this Fixlet</FONT></STRONG></LABEL></P>
<BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr><LABEL for=secret>
<P>This will upgrade Dell&nbsp;various models BIOS (Apr 2018) - This fixlet was created partly to mitigate the Intel Management Engine (Intel SA-00086) vulnerability.</P>
<P><STRONG>NOTE: The "E" in front of the model name is very important! Example - Latitude E5450 is NOT the same as Latitude 5450!! This fact applies to all Dell models, usually indicating the presence of a docking socket on the bottom of the machine. This fixlet will not apply to models other than the ones listed below.</STRONG></P>
<P>Model: Latitude&nbsp;E5450 - Upgrade to A19</P>
<P>Model: Latitude E5270/E5470/E5570 and Precision 3510 - Upgrade to&nbsp;1.18.6</P>
<P>Model: Latitude 5280/5288/5480/5488/5580 and Precision 3520 - Upgrade to 1.9.3</P>
<P>***NOTE***: BIOS version 1.9.4&nbsp;on Latitude E5470 with Windows 10 build 1607&nbsp;will not update using this fixlet. There is a problem on these machines that inhibits them from restarting from Windows to complete the&nbsp;BIOS update. Full shutdown and startup will not complete the update due to loss of power to the memory module storing the BIOS update information used at next reboot. Local update is required via Dell built in flash tool on the machine. This issue may also affect versions 01.06.XX, 01.07.XX, 01.08.XX, 1.10.X, and 1.11.X but has not been confirmed.</P>
<P><STRONG>Exit Code descriptions:</STRONG></P>
<P>Exit Code 2: Pending restart</P>
<P>Exit Code 7: Incorrect BIOS password</P>
<P>Exit Code 10: Insufficient charge of the battery (must be above 10%)</LABEL></P></BLOCKQUOTE>
<P dir=ltr><LABEL for=secret><STRONG><FONT size=3>Action Description</FONT></STRONG></LABEL></P>
<UL dir=ltr>
<LI>
<DIV style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px"><LABEL for=secret><STRONG>Action1: Upgrade Dell BIOS</STRONG></LABEL></DIV></LI></UL>
<P style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px"><LABEL for=secret></LABEL><LABEL for=secret>This action requires&nbsp;the&nbsp;BIOS password of the machines you are deplying to be typed into the "Password" field under "Customization Options". This is required if the machine BIOS is configured with a password.</LABEL></P>
<P style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr><LABEL for=secret><STRONG><FONT color=#008000 size=3>Customization Options</FONT></STRONG></LABEL></P>
<BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr>
<P><LABEL for=secret>Password:</LABEL> <INPUT id=secret type=password name=secret> <script>
                                                   document.body.ontakeaction = function() {
                                                                    var theSecret = document.getElementById( "secret" ).value;
																	if (theSecret==null || theSecret=="")
																		{alert("Hey, you forgot to enter the BIOS password! Please enter it on the Description tab before taking the action.");}
                                                                    else
																		{TakeSecureFixletAction( Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), "Action1", {}, { secret: theSecret } );}
                                                                    return false;
                                                   }
                                                   </script> </P></BLOCKQUOTE>
<P dir=ltr><STRONG><FONT color=#ff0000 size=3>Important Notes</FONT></STRONG></P>
<UL dir=ltr>
<LI>
<DIV>You must enter a password in order to take an action</DIV>
<LI>
<DIV>Because of the way secure parameters work, you cannot use this task in&nbsp;a baseline, target an action dynamically by property (e.g., automatic groups), or use/add additional actions.</DIV>
<LI>
<DIV>BitLocker is Suspended until next reboot as part of this action. No input of the key is necessary after update.</DIV></LI></UL>
<P><FONT size=2 face=Arial><STRONG>This fixlet has been verified to work when upgrading from the following BIOS versions:</STRONG></FONT></P>
<P>
